-- title:
--   Local principality at a ramified place of a right ideal
-- statement:
--   Let $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$, let $p$ be a prime, and assume `IsDefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt a b p`: $a<0$, $b<0$, and for every height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ the ring $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_v$ has all its nonzero elements invertible exactly when $p$ lies in the prime ideal of $v$. Let $\Lambda$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ which is a maximal order, i.e. $\Lambda$ contains $1$, is closed under multiplication, spans $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ and is finitely generated over $\mathbb{Z}$, and every submodule with these four properties that contains $\Lambda$ equals $\Lambda$. Let $I$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule with $I\le\Lambda$, stable under right multiplication by $\Lambda$ ($z\mu\in I$ for $z\in I$, $\mu\in\Lambda$), and of full rank in the sense that $n\Lambda\subseteq I$ for some nonzero integer $n$. Let $v$ be a height-one prime of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p\in v$. Then there is a unit $X$ of the ring $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_v$ such that for every $t$ in that ring, $t$ lies in [`Submodule.localBox I v`](def/Submodule_LocalBox.html#L40) if and only if $X^{-1}t$ lies in [`Submodule.localBox Λ v`](def/Submodule_LocalBox.html#L40), where for a submodule $M$ the additive subgroup [`Submodule.localBox M v`](def/Submodule_LocalBox.html#L40) is generated by the elementary tensors $z\otimes c$ with $z\in M$ and $c$ in the valuation ring of $\mathbb{Q}_v$.
--
--   This is the ramified-place case of the classical fact that a one-sided ideal of full rank in a maximal order of a quaternion algebra becomes principal after completion: at the place where the algebra is a division algebra, the completed order is the valuation ring of the reduced-norm valuation, and every such local ideal is generated by a single unit of the completed algebra. It feeds the construction of an adelic generator for right ideals of $\Lambda$ in [`QuaternionAlgebra.IsMaximalOrder.exists_ofFiniteIdele_eq_of_forall_mul_mem`](thm.html#QuaternionAlgebra.IsMaximalOrder.exists_ofFiniteIdele_eq_of_forall_mul_mem).
-- source:
